rage.":["u363"],"copy|Glargine or degludec supplies background insulin.":["u364"],"copy|Lispro, aspart and glulisine cover a meal, while NPH has a discernible peak.":["u365"],"copy|Consider insulin in type 2 diabetes with severe symptomatic hyperglycemia or catabolic weight loss.":["u366"],"copy|In type 1, basal insulin remains necessary to prevent ketosis.":["u367"],"copy|Before prescribing, have the patient or caregiver demonstrate injection and monitoring.":["u368"],"copy|Titrate cautiously, particularly with poor renal clearance.":["u369"],"copy|Insulin needs may fall as glucotoxicity resolves, so a dose that was appropriate weeks earlier can later cause lows (pp1581–1584, Tables 99-12 and 99-13).":["u370"],"copy|Two ADA 2022 questions used different insulin decisions.":["u371"],"copy|In June 2023 Q24, untreated symptomatic hyperglycemia, dementia and weight loss favor a simple once-daily basal regimen with caregiver support.":["u372"],"copy|In Q70, the patient was at an A1C of 7.0% on basal insulin and three 6-unit mealtime injections.":["u373"],"copy|Figure 13.1 allows discontinuation of meal doses of 10 units or less and addition of a noninsulin agent with monitoring.":["u374"],"copy|For doses above 10 units, its initial step is to halve the dose while introducing the noninsulin agent.":["u375"],"copy|Sitagliptin can replace the small Apidra doses without sacrificing the indications for the statin or empagliflozin.":["u376"],"copy|ADA 2022, Figure 13.1 and Table 13.2":["u377"],"copy|HHS versus DKA.":["u378"],"copy|Severe insulin deficiency permits lipolysis, ketone production and metabolic acidosis in DKA.":["u379"],"copy|Replace insulin, fluid and electrolyte losses and seek the precipitant.":["u380"],"copy|In HHS, extreme glucose-driven diuresis produces hyperosmolality, dehydration, renal insufficiency and neurologic changes, with little ketosis.":["u381"],"copy|The June 2026 Basic patient had glucose 850 mg/dL, measured osmolality 393 mOsm/kg, hypernatremia, confusion and barely detectable ketones.":["u382"],"copy|Restore volume and correct sodium and osmolality carefully, with monitoring for cardiac overload and treatment of the underlying illness.":["u383"],"copy|In the postoperative 2020 patient, marked ketonuria pointed instead toward SGLT2-associated DKA (pp1580, 1585).":["u384"],"copy|Long-term care and hospice.":["u385"],"copy|Match rapid insulin to food actually eaten if intake is erratic, and ensure the facility can recognize and treat lows.":["u386"],"copy|Avoid restrictive diets that aggravate poor intake.":["u387"],"copy|Table 99-16 distinguishes relatively stable disease, advanced disease with months remaining, deterioration over weeks and the last days.":["u388"],"copy|With months of prognosis, simplify the regimen and liberalize food choices.":["u389"],"copy|With weeks, agree on less burdensome targets and avoid long-acting sulfonylureas.":["u390"],"copy|In the last days, reduce or stop testing and drugs as appropriate to diabetes type and symptoms.":["u391"],"copy|Type 1 still requires some insulin to prevent distressing ketoacidosis (pp1585–1586, Table 99-16).":["u392"],"copy|Preserve muscle and function while managing glucose.":["u393"],"copy|A healthier older adult with central obesity may benefit from modest caloric restriction combined with exercise.":["u394"],"copy|Frailty, weight loss or poor intake favor adequate energy and protein, access to regular meals and coordination with insulin.":["u395"],"copy|Ask who buys and prepares food, whether the patient can chew and swallow, and whether depression, finances or transportation limit intake.":["u396"],"copy|Dietary supplements have not convincingly improved hyperglycemia or diabetes complications in this context (pp1575–1576, Tables 99-9 and 99-10).":["u397"],"copy|The first visit assesses ADLs and IADLs, cognition, mood, falls, nutrition, blood pressure including standing measurements, feet, vision and renal function.":["u398"],"copy|Review medicines that raise glucose or impair recognition of lows.":["u399"],"copy|Type 2 predominates in older adults.":["u400"],"copy|Type 1 reflects severe insulin deficiency and can persist from youth.":["u401"],"copy|Pancreatic destruction, glucocorticoids, hormone excess and prior gestational diabetes indicate other diagnostic or risk pathways.":["u402"],"copy|Chronic glycemia damages small vessels, while common vascular risk factors compound large-vessel disease (pp1559–1565, 1567–1568).":["u403"],"copy|Coordinate primary care, endocrinology, nursing education, nutrition, eye and foot care according to complexity.":["u404"],"copy|Review actual glucose records, hypoglycemia, medication execution, diet, exercise, interval illness and goals.":["u405"],"copy|Disease duration and life expectancy determine how much delayed benefit is plausible.":["u406"],"copy|Population quality indicators that count A1C or BP thresholds can miss falls, severe lows, hypotension and patient burden.":["u407"],"copy|The individual's functioning and preferences guide the visit (pp1569–1570, 1582–1583, Tables 99-5 and 99-13).":["u408"],"copy|איך מתרגמים את המעקב לביקור בקהילה.":["u409"],"copy|משרד הבריאות מתאר ארבע דרכים לאבחון סוכרת.":["u410"],"copy|הן כוללות HbA1c של 6.5% ומעלה, גלוקוז בצום של שמונה שעות מ־126 מ״ג/ד״ל, שעתיים אחרי העמסת 75 גרם מ־200, או גלוקוז אקראי מ־200 עם תסמינים אופייניים או משבר.":["u411"],"copy|בבדיקת הרגליים האחות בודקת את העור ואת התחושה ומדריכה לגבי טיפול בכפות הרגליים.":["u412"],"copy|רופא עיניים בודק את קרקעית העין, ודיאטנית מתאימה תפריט ופעילות.":["u413"],"copy|משרד הבריאות, סוכרת סוג 2, 09.10.2024, סעיפי האבחון והמעקב":["u414"],"copy|כשהתיאבון יורד או שהמטופל מחמיץ ארוחות.":["u415"],"copy|מתאימים את זמני הארוחות ואת כמות הפחמימות לטיפול, בודקים ירידה לא רצויה במשקל וסיכון לאובדן שריר ומשלבים חלבון לאורך היום.":["u416"],"copy|כאשר הגלוקוז מתחת ל־70 מ״ג/ד״ל והאדם ער ויכול לבלוע בבטחה, ההנחיה היא בדרך כלל 15 גרם פחמימה מהירת ספיגה, בדיקה לאחר 15 דקות וחזרה על הטיפול אם הערך עדיין נמוך.":["u417"],"copy|בהפרעה בהכרה או בבליעה נמנעים ממתן דרך הפה ומזעיקים עזרה דחופה.":["u418"],"copy|אירועים חוזרים מצדיקים התאמה מחדש של התרופות והתזונה.":["u419"],"copy|משרד הבריאות, תזונה וסוכרת בגיל המבוגר, 24.11.2026, סעיפי פחמימות, מסת השריר והיפוגליקמיה":["u420"],"copy|The chapter gives annual follow-up after a borderline cognitive screen and every 2–3 years after a normal screen (p1568). ADA 2026 recommends an initial screen and annual screening from age 65, with additional assessment when self-management changes.":["u29"],"copy|Hazzard gives a BP goal below 140/90 mmHg for most (p1572). ADA 2026 recommends below 130/80 mmHg when safely attainable. For poor health, limited life expectancy or high treatment risk, a goal such as below 140/90 may be appropriate. Check standing BP (ADA 2026, recommendation 13.9).":["u35"]}}
